# The publisher's own archive files, vendored byte-for-byte under
# data/corpus/. Git must never normalise them.
#
# THE DEFECT THIS PREVENTS: this repository is developed on Windows with
# core.autocrlf=true, so git would store these with LF and hand them back as
# CRLF — and a clone configured any other way would get different bytes. The
# SHA-256 recorded for each file in data/corpus.lock.json is of these exact
# bytes, so a line-ending conversion anywhere in the round trip makes every
# digest mismatch and reports the publisher's own Scripture as altered. It is
# the same trap CLAUDE.md rule 24 names for comparing a deployment.
data/corpus/** -text

# Derived Bible data is generated, compared by hash, and served as-is.
data/bible/** -text
